ia_006_fan_chopper_cmfb: the fixed snapshot records normalized composition by
Noorizadeh (MacAnalog group), using the Fan CCIA and transistor CMFB blocks.
No separate component license tag is supplied; original/normalized database
materials retain PolyForm Noncommercial terms and the Required Notice above.
Layout-Bench retains all 46 MOS groups with maintained parallel fingering and
explicit process-grid rounding of CMFB dimensions, externalizes four bias
voltages and the common-mode reference, exposes two summing-node monitors,
implements all passives with 13 MIM units and 90 high-poly segments, retunes
Miller/controller compensation, adds taps and independently constructs the
matched physical witness and full-clock measurement deck. The independently
authored measurement deck is MIT; circuit derivatives are not relicensed MIT.

smp_001_nmos_th: the fixed manifest records a SpiceXplorer worked example,
analog-circuit-design provenance and an Apache-2.0 component label. Applicable
Apache terms remain in LICENSE alongside the database PolyForm Noncommercial
