amp_012_peng_tcfc and amp_015_sau_cfcc: CODA-Team AnalogGym BSD-3-Clause
provenance at the fixed snapshot. Layout-Bench retains all 32/24 source MOS
groups, respectively, rounds dimensions to the 10 nm grid and regroups
parallel fingers while preserving each group's rounded total W and L.
The maintained circuits contain 108/225 physical MOS and preserve separate
source-tied input wells, all original active paths and compensation branches.
AMP012 adds approximately 4 pF net10-output MIM compensation and calibrates
the external sink from 1.29849 to 0.16231125 uA. AMP015 adds approximately
16 pF net050-output compensation and 48 pF output-to-return storage, and
calibrates its sink from 10.0474 to 1.255925 uA. Three/seventeen physical MIM
units implement all capacitors. Taps, witnesses and native measurement decks
are independently authored. Normalized circuit derivatives and witnesses
retain PolyForm terms and the Required Notice; measurement decks are MIT.

ldo_001_analoggym_basic: CODA-Team AnalogGym BSD-3-Clause provenance at the
fixed snapshot. Layout-Bench retains all 24 MOS groups and exact per-group
total W/L, regrouping 1,168 source fingers into 831 physical MOS, including
the unchanged 464-finger PMOS pass array. Three MIM units retain the original
net106-output compensation, one added MIM supplies approximately 4 pF at
net10-output, and sixteen high-poly segments implement the 300/100 kohm
divider. The external reference is deliberately changed from 0.4 to 0.225 V;
the 8 uA sink and internal bias paths remain. The zero-volt measurement link
moves to the explicit divider/input interface. Physical taps, witness and
native loop/regulation/startup decks are independently authored. Normalized
circuit derivatives and the witness retain PolyForm terms and the Required
Notice; independently authored measurement decks are MIT.

VREF001 mixed-device reference
-----------------------------
vref_001_vgs retains the fixed-source LV/HV two-NMOS VGS reference, including
original W/L and gate/source connections. The fixed manifest calls it a
SpiceXplorer worked example, identifies analog-circuit-design provenance and
labels the component Apache-2.0. This does not relicense the normalized
analog-db material as a whole: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0, the Required Notice
and applicable component terms in LICENSE remain in force. Layout-Bench resolves
parameters, adds physical substrate contacts, supplies an independent GDS and
a separately MIT-identified native measurement deck. No external provenance
pointer was followed to acquire additional circuit material.
